 the Microsoft Push Notification Service to an app running on Windows Phone. The format and meaning of the data is determined by the app.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1612764">raw notification</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1639923">અપૂર્ણ સૂચના</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31699_1612765_1639932"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To purchase an app just before downloading and installing it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1612765">purchase at download</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1639932">ડાઉનલોડ પર ખરીદો</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="317_141659_1944485"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An XML vocabulary that is used to transform XML data to another form, such as HTML, by means of a style sheet that defines presentation rules.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141659">Extensible Stylesheet Language</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1944485">એક્સટેન્સિબલ સ્ટાઇલશીટ લેંગ્વેજ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="317_141659_496157"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An XML vocabulary that is used to transform XML data to another form, such as HTML, by means of a style sheet that defines presentation rules.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141659">Extensible Stylesheet Language</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="496157">XSL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="317_141660_1944485"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An XML vocabulary that is used to transform XML data to another form, such as HTML, by means of a style sheet that defines presentation rules.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141660">XSL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1944485">એક્સટેન્સિબલ સ્ટાઇલશીટ લેંગ્વેજ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="317_141660_496157"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An XML vocabulary that is used to transform XML data to another form, such as HTML, by means of a style sheet that defines presentation rules.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141660">XSL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="496157">XSL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3170_783225_2929925"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A touch-sensitive screen on your device that can recognize the location of a touch (of a fingertip or stylus, for example) on its surface and translate that touch into a desired action (such as opening an item or moving the cursor).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="783225">touchscreen</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929925">ટચસ્ક્રીન</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31700_1612766_1639917"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To purchase an app after downloading, installing and trying it out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1612766">purchase after trial</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1639917">અજમાયશ પછી ખરીદો</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31701_1612767_1766887"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An image uploaded by the developer that Microsoft can use as a part of promotion via Featured lists and/or marketing campaigns.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1612767">promotional image</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1766887">પ્રમોશનલ ઇમેજ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31703_1612776_1639812"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The money a developer receives from app and add-on sales in the Windows Store, including advertising revenue.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1612776">payout</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1639812">પેઆઉટ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31705_1612778_1640000"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To move an application into the store. Involves the uploading and certification of an app's packages and listing data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1612778">onboard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1640000">ઑનબોર્ડ ક