The Windows app that can run a variety of manufacturing and hardware tools, tests, and tasks during the OEM device bring-up and manufacturing process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2898945">Factory Orchestrator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899439">ફેક્ટરી ઓરછેસ્ટ્રેટોર</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51505_2899583_2900024"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams for Education that provides the user with at-a-glance data views to help them monitor their students' Teams activity, including overall digital engagement, assignment turn-in, communication activity, and grade distribution and trends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899583">Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900024">Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51505_2899583_2949461"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams for Education that provides the user with at-a-glance data views to help them monitor their students' Teams activity, including overall digital engagement, assignment turn-in, communication activity, and grade distribution and trends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899583">Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2949461">શિક્ષણ Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51505_2949265_2900024"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams for Education that provides the user with at-a-glance data views to help them monitor their students' Teams activity, including overall digital engagement, assignment turn-in, communication activity, and grade distribution and trends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2949265">Education Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900024">Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51505_2949265_2949461"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams for Education that provides the user with at-a-glance data views to help them monitor their students' Teams activity, including overall digital engagement, assignment turn-in, communication activity, and grade distribution and trends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2949265">Education Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2949461">શિક્ષણ Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51506_2899584_2900028"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The video conferencing mode in Microsoft Teams in which participants' video feeds are combined on the screen in such a way as to give the participants the impression that they are all in the same physical space together.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899584">Together mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900028">એક સાથે મોડ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51507_2899585_2900025"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The view in Microsoft Teams that allows the user to see up to 49 video feeds at once.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899585">Large gallery</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900025">મોટી ગેલેરી</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51508_2899586_2900023"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The view in Microsoft Teams that allows the user to see up to 9 video feeds at once.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899586">Gallery</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900023">ગેલેરી</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51509_2899587_2900026"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A billing model wherein an associated payment method is charged automatically over set periods of time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899587">recurring billing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900026">પુનરાવર્તિત બિલિંગ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5151_228751_496420"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A real-time communication session between two or more users, which can involve IM, video, or audio.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="228751">conversation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="496420">વાતચીત</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51510_2899588_2900027"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of all-in-one dedicated Teams devices featuring an ambient touchscreen and a hands-free experience powered by Cortana that brings together the user's favorite Teams features: chat, meetings, calls, calendar, and files into a single device, promoting human connection in the remote workplace.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899588">Teams display</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900027">Teams પ્રદર્શન</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51543_2900640_2901001"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams that provides the user with analytics about teams that they are a member or owner of, including data about user and guest volume as well as messaging activity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900640">Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2901001">Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51563_2901221_2901707"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A third-party device (such as a camera, headset, phone, or room accessory) that has been certified via the Microsoft device Certification Program to provide a compatible experience when used with specific Microsoft software.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2901221">certified device</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2901707">પ્રમાણિત ઉપકરણ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51578_2901804_2902061"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Feature (either built into Windows or available as the Windows Lookup app) to allow users to select a word or group of words and look up more information, definition or translation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2901804">Lookup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902061">લુકઅપ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_154233_496240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="154233">Layer Two Tunneling Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="496240">લેયર ટુ ટનલિંગ પ્રોટોકૉલ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_154233_496892"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="154233">Layer Two Tunneling Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="496892">L2TP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_318115_496240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318115">L2TP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="496240">લેયર ટુ ટનલિંગ પ્રોટોકૉલ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_318115_496892"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318115">L2TP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="496892">L2TP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51586_2902141_2902800"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A style in Word that shows t